The user asks "when the space/square doesn't have the data we don't hover". Maybe the actual behavior they observed: hovering over the whole map shows popups on tracts that are outside the scored data because `tracts` includes only features with layers values... wait, actually look:

```js
features: shapes.features.flatMap((f) => {
  const values = layers?.[f.properties.geoid];
  return values ? [{ ...f, properties: { ...f.properties, ...values } }] : [];
}),
```

So no-data tracts are not in source at all. Hmm, so hovering them gives nothing. Unless `layers` includes all geoids but with values of fit for only some? computeLayers skips undefined audience.

Maybe the user means the opposite: the popup shows for areas with data, but they'd like no hover on empty space? Maybe there's a cursor style... Let me look at map-panel for hint text and maybe pointer.

